Usage: xnvme qublk <command> [<args>]

Expose an xNVMe device as a ublk block-device

Where <command> is one of:

  serve            | Serve a ublk block-device for each of the given xNVMe devices
  del              | Delete a ublk device left behind by a killed server

See 'xnvme qublk <command> --help' for the description of [<args>]
See 'xnvme qublk --version' for the library version and the revision it was built from

qublk - ublk server backed by xNVMe -- ver: {major: 0, minor: 7, patch: 5, vcs: 'be83e57'}
